    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **290 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the rule: creating an owner is rejected with **400** when the owner's city already contains 8 owners.\n\n**Production change** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n- Added a guard in `addOwner` (right after the daily-registration-limit check) returning `HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST` when the city is full.\n- Added `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 8` and a `hasReachedCityOwnerLimit(String city)` helper that counts owners whose city matches via the existing `normalize(...)` idiom (case- and whitespace-insensitive), mirroring the established `hasReachedDailyRegistrationLimit` / `nextCustomerCode` patterns.\n\n**Tests** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`:\n- Added `createOwnerRejectedWhenCityFull` (8 owners in a city \u2192 9th POST is 400) and `createOwnerAllowedBelowCityLimit` (7 owners \u2192 8th POST is 201).\n- Updated the two existing daily-limit tests, which seeded 19\u201320 owners all in \"Madison\" (one expecting `isCreated()`). That directly conflicted with the new 8-per-city cap, so they now seed each owner in a distinct city (`DailyCity-<i>`), isolating them to the daily-limit concern.\n\nExisting single-owner Madison POST tests were unaffected \u2014 the seed data has only 4 Madison owners and each test adds one and rolls back via `@Transactional`.",
